WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.834
-Welcome back.
-Thanks, Jimmy.

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:04.400
-It is so good to see you.
You look fantastic.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:05.767
-Thanks.

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:07.968
-You know, I have talked to you
about a lot of things,

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:09.534
but I saw you posted over
the weekend --

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:14.667
You were at "SNL" with Tony Hawk
here and Amy Poehler.

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:15.868
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:16.901
I didn't know you guys
were pro skaters.

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:17.901
-I know.
-Yeah, it was good to know.

00:00:17.901 --> 00:00:19.100
-Isn't that something?

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.601
A lot of people don't know that
about Amy and I,

00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:23.601
but we spend most of
our time doing, you know,

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:24.834
skateboarding stuff.

00:00:24.834 --> 00:00:27.200
-Were you there just for fun
or to see the gang

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.334
or so -- Aubrey.

00:00:28.334 --> 00:00:30.467
-Got to support Aubrey,
the baby.

00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:31.567
-The baby was great.

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:32.801
-Gotta support the baby,
who crushed.

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:33.934
-She did.

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:35.300
You crushed when you hosted,
by the way.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:36.501
-Oh!
-Yes, you crushed!

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:38.434
-These are crushers.
-You crushed!

00:00:38.434 --> 00:00:41.801
-We go in and we crush.
-You know to how to do it!

00:00:41.801 --> 00:00:43.868
-But we talked right before
you were about to host,

00:00:43.868 --> 00:00:44.968
and you were kind of like,

00:00:44.968 --> 00:00:46.133
"Dude,
I'm so excited about this."

00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:47.934
-Yeah, and you told me to
pull out, remember?

00:00:47.934 --> 00:00:49.267
-Yeah, I said --
-You were like, "Baby, baby."

00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:51.300
-I said, "Hey, cancel.
They'll get somebody else."

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.467
-"You take the money, pull out."

00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:55.267
But I did it anyway.

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:56.434
-Yeah, you did.
-I don't listen.

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:57.868
-Yeah. You're a rebel.

00:00:57.868 --> 00:01:00.634
-I think maybe that was
the greatest week of my life.

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:02.067
-You think so?

00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:05.167
-Yeah, Baby Freddie and Maya.
-You got to play with everybody.

00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:06.200
-Yes.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.234
-You were so good,
like a natural.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.133
But then you went back, too.
-Oh, I know.

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:13.334
I got a Bat-Signal call to be
"Hello Kitty" with Keke.

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:14.901
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:14.901 --> 00:01:19.400
That's a rite of passage as
a New Yorker, to get that call.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:20.634
-I want to ask you
about something.

00:01:20.634 --> 00:01:23.334
-Okay. I know you recently --

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:25.300
You had that amnesia thing
come up, so you just go slow.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:26.534
-Yeah, I hit my head
before the show,

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:27.901
and I don't remember who I am.

00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:29.634
-Yeah, just do your own pace.
-So that's my question.

00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:30.701
-Yes, dear?
-Who am I?

00:01:30.701 --> 00:01:31.767
-Yeah. Listen --

00:01:31.767 --> 00:01:33.267
-Who am I to you, though,
seriously?

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:35.601
-Jimmy, on the deepest level,
who are any of us, you feel me?

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:37.734
-Wow!
-That's right.

00:01:37.734 --> 00:01:39.267
-Let me take a hit of that.

00:01:39.267 --> 00:01:41.400
-The thing is --
If you guys want some of this.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.467
-Yeah. Come on.

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:43.968
-But, like,
what are we doing here?

00:01:43.968 --> 00:01:45.033
Where are we? Midtown?

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:46.834
-I have a real serious
question here

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:49.033
and I want to know -- I want to
get down to the nitty-gritty.

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:50.133
-Okay, my dear.

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:52.133
-Are you --
You have a new hobby.

00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:53.467
Is this true?

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:55.067
And what I'm hearing --
Do you know where I'm going?

00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:58.868
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.
So I guess word is spreading.

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:01.534
So, in addition to
the skateboarding,

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:04.167
you know, in a new year,
you want to reflect.

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:06.100
You want to consider,
"Who am I?"

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.634
-"What is this?"
-I decided -- I thought --

00:02:08.634 --> 00:02:10.300
I think my
whole personality was bad.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:12.167
-That's unbelievable.
I've never heard of that.

00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:13.467
-You know what I mean?

00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:15.534
What am I doing with New York
and the cigarettes?

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:17.467
Enough. So I became a surfer.

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:18.868
And I think maybe --

00:02:18.868 --> 00:02:20.400
-You became a surfer.
-Yeah.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.167
-In my whole life,
I never would've thought

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:23.701
Natasha Lyonne would surf.

00:02:23.701 --> 00:02:27.400
And we've known each other
since 1990-something.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:31.033
And -- The first time we met,
Kurt Cobain was there.

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:32.367
-That's right.

00:02:32.367 --> 00:02:35.601
-And you -- But how did you
even get into surfing?

00:02:35.601 --> 00:02:36.834
What do you do?
Aren't you nervous?

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:38.834
-Well, I Googled
"mid-life crisis."

00:02:38.834 --> 00:02:41.334
And I --

00:02:41.334 --> 00:02:44.834
-Ah, exactly. I do it every day.

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:47.133
-So, I thought,
"I think I'll take this one."

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:51.334
And, you know, make me, like,
a Buddhist or something.

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:54.334
"I'm too into quantum physics,
I should be more into nature,"

00:02:54.334 --> 00:02:55.400
I said to myself.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.334
-Wow!
So this makes you more Zen.

00:02:57.334 --> 00:02:59.434
-Yes. And now I'm, like --
I get up all the time.

00:02:59.434 --> 00:03:01.701
I know I don't seem it,
but I'm quite spry.

00:03:01.701 --> 00:03:03.334
And I go out there --

00:03:03.334 --> 00:03:04.701
-You're up
and you're on the board.

00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:06.434
-I'm out there.
And it's very hard.

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:09.133
You can't -- It's hard to
light up if you're on the board.

00:03:09.133 --> 00:03:10.267
-Yeah.

00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:12.133
-So it's very helpful,
just as a tip

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:13.400
for anyone struggling to quit.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.000
-You want to quit smoking,
just start surfing.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.167
-That's the ticket.
-That's the way to do it.

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:18.234
-It's been great. Yeah.

00:03:18.234 --> 00:03:19.334
-I can't believe
that you're doing this.

00:03:19.334 --> 00:03:20.501
This is so cool.
-Yeah.

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:21.868
-And you're going to continue
to do this?

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:24.801
-I think that's who I am now.
Yeah, basically. Yeah.

00:03:24.801 --> 00:03:26.467
-That's --
You're a complete surfer now?

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:28.100
-That's just --
Yeah, that's who I am.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.734
New show,
new personality, you know?

00:03:30.734 --> 00:03:32.701
-Well, what about the old show?
What about "Russian Doll"?

00:03:32.701 --> 00:03:34.234
-"Russian Doll"
is still in the mix.

00:03:34.234 --> 00:03:35.834
So, "Russian Doll" -- But that's
when I'm going to do --

00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:38.968
-That's not surfing Natasha.
-Yeah, but that's -- It is.

00:03:38.968 --> 00:03:40.267
It is.
-It is now?

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:42.501
-Yeah. You know, like,
string theory, surfing.

00:03:42.501 --> 00:03:44.033
It's a different kind.
-Ooh.

00:03:44.033 --> 00:03:45.901
-Yeah, you got to surf
a different kind of a wave.

00:03:45.901 --> 00:03:47.067
You see?
-Wow! Ooh!

00:03:47.067 --> 00:03:48.434
-Yeah, but --
-This is so deep.

00:03:48.434 --> 00:03:50.767
-I know. Life is heavy.
-Yeah.

00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:52.667
-You know, we all die,
so it's nuts.

00:03:52.667 --> 00:03:54.801
-Yeah, no, don't get that deep.
"Russian Doll."

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:56.300
-Oh, not us.
-No, not us.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:57.901
-I meant everyone else.
-Yeah.

00:03:57.901 --> 00:04:00.100
-Yeah, don't panic. Yes, dear?

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:02.300
-With my plastic surgeon,
I don't die.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:03.901
Yeah, of course. Hello.
-By the way, you look so good.

00:04:03.901 --> 00:04:06.300
-Thank you so much.
-You are honestly so good.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.067
-Thank you so much.
-Yeah.

00:04:08.067 --> 00:04:10.167
-Do I look like mid-50s?
-No.

00:04:10.167 --> 00:04:13.200
I would say -- I thought --
See, if you're 27,

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:17.334
that makes me like 22, which...

00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:21.267
Yeah. As I always say,
not a day over 1.

00:04:21.267 --> 00:04:22.868
That's how you look.
-I appreciate that.

00:04:22.868 --> 00:04:24.234
But, so, "Russian Doll" --

00:04:24.234 --> 00:04:25.834
we're not sure
when that's coming back.

00:04:25.834 --> 00:04:27.934
-I got to write it.
I got to clone myself.

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.367
I don't know if
the science is there.

00:04:29.367 --> 00:04:31.434
I got a lot of projects.
-You got a lot of projects.

00:04:31.434 --> 00:04:34.234
-If I don't direct three movies
before it's over,

00:04:34.234 --> 00:04:36.968
I'll have a bad "All That Jazz"
moment looking back, so...

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:38.868
-You think so?
-Yeah, I got to set myself up.

00:04:38.868 --> 00:04:40.667
This is -- You know,
you've got to feel like

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:42.200
a narrow window as an artist.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:44.667
You got to get it all in before
they take it away from you.

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:46.667
That's show biz. It's --
-Do you want to direct?

00:04:46.667 --> 00:04:47.934
Do you want to direct?
-Yeah.

00:04:47.934 --> 00:04:50.534
Yeah, I did all that directing
on "Russian Doll,"

00:04:50.534 --> 00:04:51.634
and I loved it.

00:04:51.634 --> 00:04:53.000
And --
-I could -- I love this.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.267
-Yeah, it makes me so happy.

00:04:54.267 --> 00:04:55.734
It's really --
It's a joy in my life.

00:04:55.734 --> 00:04:57.267
-So we're going to see some
Natasha Lyonne-directed movies.

00:04:57.267 --> 00:04:58.534
-Yeah, "pictures,"
I'm gonna call them.

00:04:58.534 --> 00:05:01.000
-Yeah, "pictures!"
That's what I'm talking about.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.734
I would love that.
-Yeah.

00:05:02.734 --> 00:05:04.000
-Oh, you've got to
come back for that.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:05.400
I will support that all the way.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.133
-Let's talk about "Poker Face."
-Let's get to business.

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:08.200
-"Poker Face."
-Yeah.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.567
-It's on Peacock.

00:05:09.567 --> 00:05:11.167
And if you don't have Peacock,
get it.

00:05:11.167 --> 00:05:12.300
It's a fantastic service.
-It's -- Yeah.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:13.467
This show is excellent.

00:05:13.467 --> 00:05:14.467
It's Rian Johnson.
I mean, it's excellent.

00:05:14.467 --> 00:05:15.601
-Oh, I thought you meant
my show.

00:05:15.601 --> 00:05:16.601
I was going to say,
"Thank you so much."

00:05:16.601 --> 00:05:18.100
-Oh, by the way,
this show is also great.

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:19.834
-Thank you. I appreciate it.
Rian Johnson created it.

00:05:19.834 --> 00:05:21.200
-Yeah.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:23.467
-No, but Rian Johnson also
created your show, "Poker Face."

00:05:23.467 --> 00:05:24.534
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:24.534 --> 00:05:25.968
-We know Rian Johnson
from, recently --

00:05:25.968 --> 00:05:28.033
-As the director of...
-"Knives Out."

00:05:28.033 --> 00:05:29.033
-...this show.

00:05:29.033 --> 00:05:30.033
-And, of course,
"The Tonight Show,"

00:05:30.033 --> 00:05:31.033
as well, yeah.

00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:32.234
Rian and I go way back.

00:05:32.234 --> 00:05:34.701
-And he got an
Academy Award nomination

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:35.701
this morning for "Glass Onion."

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:36.834
-Not too shabby.
-Not too shabby.

00:05:36.834 --> 00:05:38.367
-Not too shabby.
Congrats, Rian Johnson.

00:05:38.367 --> 00:05:39.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:39.601 --> 00:05:42.601
Seem like a fun --
-This is a mensch of a guy.

00:05:42.601 --> 00:05:45.634
-He seems like a fun individual.
-A genuine genius.

00:05:45.634 --> 00:05:47.300
I mean -- You know, we talk
a lot about the crossword.

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:48.334
I can only do the Thursday.

00:05:48.334 --> 00:05:49.501
He does Friday, Saturday
no problem.

00:05:49.501 --> 00:05:52.968
-You do Thursday? Really?
-Oh, I do Thursdays.

00:05:52.968 --> 00:05:56.667
And -- Oh, also Hong Chau
and Stephanie Hsu

00:05:56.667 --> 00:05:59.067
were nominated this morning,
and they're guest stars in it.

00:05:59.067 --> 00:06:00.367
They're awesome.

00:06:00.367 --> 00:06:01.801
-By the way, the guest stars
on "Poker Face" --

00:06:01.801 --> 00:06:03.067
-Bananas.

00:06:03.067 --> 00:06:05.033
-The guest stars on your show
is kind of insane.

00:06:05.033 --> 00:06:06.133
-Yeah.
-Can we go through some of them?

00:06:06.133 --> 00:06:07.567
-Sure, sure.
-Chloe Sevigny.

00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:09.167
-Aw, that's my buddy.
That's my sister.

00:06:09.167 --> 00:06:10.367
-She's the best.
-Yeah.

00:06:10.367 --> 00:06:12.467
-I love that she's in it.
Who else showed up in it?

00:06:12.467 --> 00:06:13.934
Who's your --
Who's the villain in this?

00:06:13.934 --> 00:06:15.234
-Oh, we got Benjamin Bratt.

00:06:15.234 --> 00:06:16.567
-Benjamin Bratt
is fantastic in this.

00:06:16.567 --> 00:06:19.200
-A gem of a human being. Yeah.
-Who else showed up?

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:20.767
There's, like --
-We got Adrien Brody.

00:06:20.767 --> 00:06:22.000
Nick Nolte
is in the episode I --

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.367
-Nick Nolte is the best.
-Yeah.

00:06:23.367 --> 00:06:25.601
-I go, "How did --"
-I directed that episode.

00:06:25.601 --> 00:06:27.901
Directed Nolte, baby.
-Yes! Come on, baby!

00:06:27.901 --> 00:06:30.234
Directing Nick Nolte!
-Yeah.

00:06:30.234 --> 00:06:31.901
-It's so good.
-Judith Light.

00:06:31.901 --> 00:06:33.901
It just goes --
Joseph Gordon-Levitt.

00:06:33.901 --> 00:06:35.567
I mean, it's on and on.
-Joseph Gordon -- I know --

00:06:35.567 --> 00:06:38.000
-Lil Rel.
I mean, it's an incredible cast.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.634
-They do it because
they love you.

00:06:39.634 --> 00:06:41.100
-Aww!
-As we all do.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.734
Yeah, we would do
anything for you.

00:06:42.734 --> 00:06:44.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
Surfing or not surfing.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:45.300
-Yeah.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:48.334
-But how do we describe
"Poker Face" besides

00:06:48.334 --> 00:06:49.434
high octane?

00:06:49.434 --> 00:06:51.033
-Yeah.
Well, everything is high octane.

00:06:51.033 --> 00:06:54.100
-Everything is high octane.
-Well, it's sort of a throwback.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:56.367
It's almost like
a '70s sort of --

00:06:56.367 --> 00:07:00.801
It's if Columbo made a baby with
The Hulk and Magnum P.I.

00:07:00.801 --> 00:07:02.934
and the Angela Lansbury.

00:07:02.934 --> 00:07:04.868
-Yeah, that's exactly right.

00:07:04.868 --> 00:07:07.133
-But it looks, because of Rian,
almost like

00:07:07.133 --> 00:07:08.667
"California Split"
or "The Long Goodbye."

00:07:08.667 --> 00:07:11.300
You know, those '70s Altmans.
I mean, it's gorgeous.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:13.000
-Yeah.
-And it's just really cool.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:15.834
So, it's like
brand-new sort of throwback

00:07:15.834 --> 00:07:17.767
and it's a real
Case of the Week mystery,

00:07:17.767 --> 00:07:20.200
beautifully crafted
puzzle box each week.

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:21.834
You can watch it with
your children

00:07:21.834 --> 00:07:23.467
and also your grandparents.

00:07:23.467 --> 00:07:25.167
I'm still talking.
-I love it.

00:07:25.167 --> 00:07:26.901
-Yeah.
-I want to show a clip.

00:07:26.901 --> 00:07:28.634
Here's Natasha Lyonne in
"Poker Face."

00:07:28.634 --> 00:07:29.734
Take a look at this.

00:07:29.734 --> 00:07:32.400
-Now, you might say
that's impossible.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:34.033
The door was
locked from the inside,

00:07:34.033 --> 00:07:37.000
but that's where the
cinnamon floss comes into play.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:41.067
-Right. Cinnamon floss.

00:07:41.067 --> 00:07:42.367
I guess I'm not over
the part where

00:07:42.367 --> 00:07:43.801
you're a human lie detector.

00:07:43.801 --> 00:07:46.467
-Yeah, I know,
it's, uh -- it's crazy, but --

00:07:46.467 --> 00:07:48.167
-My favorite color is yellow.

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:50.133
-[ Chuckles ]
Bull[bleep]

00:07:50.133 --> 00:07:51.667
-I grew up in Old Dime Box.

00:07:51.667 --> 00:07:53.868
-Bull[bleep]
-I grew up in Tanglewood.

00:07:53.868 --> 00:07:56.000
-[ Chuckles ]

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:57.767
-Wow!

00:07:59.567 --> 00:08:01.467
You ever gamble?
'Cause you could make a killing.

00:08:01.467 --> 00:08:04.167
-[ Laughs ]

00:08:04.167 --> 00:08:05.334
Nah.

